    [
      "heading",
      1,
      "drive-utility",
      [
        [
          "text",
          "Drive Utility"
        ]
      ]
    ],
    [
      "block",
      "paragraph",
      [
        [
          "text",
          "Drive Utility is a general GTK disk utility included with MiniOS. It can write an existing disk image, create an image from a physical device, format a whole device, or erase it. It is not limited to MiniOS media and it is not a replacement for MiniOS Installer."
        ]
      ]
    ],
    [
      "block",
      "paragraph",
      [
        [
          "text",
          "Open it from the application menu under "
        ],
        [
          "span",
          "strong",
          [
            [
              "text",
              "System"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          "text",
          ", or run:"
        ]
      ]
    ],
    [
      "code_block",
      "driveutility",
      "bash",
      [
        [
          "syntax",
          "driveutility",
          "#6F42C1",
          "#B392F0"
        ]
      ]
    ],
    [
      "heading",
      2,
      "safety",
      [
        [
          "text",
          "Safety"
        ]
      ]
    ],
    [
      "block",
      "paragraph",
      [
        [
          "text",
          "Writing an image, formatting, and wiping are destructive operations. Verify the target by device, model, and capacity before confirming. Keep backups of anything important and disconnect unrelated removable drives when practical."
        ]
      ]
    ],
    [
      "block",
      "paragraph",
      [
        [
          "text",
          "Mounted disks are hidden by default. You can explicitly show them, but Drive Utility warns before destructive use and the backend attempts to unmount the selected device and its partitions before changing it. If the mount state is ambiguous or a filesystem remains mounted, the operation fails instead of continuing underneath an active filesystem."
        ]
      ]
    ],
    [
      "heading",
      2,
      "write-an-image",
      [
        [
          "text",
          "Write an image"
        ]
      ]
    ],
    [
      "block",
      "paragraph",
      [
        [
          "text",
          ""
        ],
        [
          "span",
          "strong",
          [
            [
              "text",
              "Write"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          "text",
          " copies an image byte-for-byte to the selected device. Compressed image input is detected by the backend where supported."
        ]
      ]
    ],
    [
      "block",
      "paragraph",
      [
        [
          "text",
          "Typical uses include writing a MiniOS ISO to USB or SD media and restoring a previously created whole-device image."
        ],
        [
          "text",
          "\n"
        ],
        [
          "text",
          "For a MiniOS ISO, this is a raw image write. It copies the ISO partition and boot layout exactly as stored in the image. It does "
        ],
        [
          "span",
          "strong",
          [
            [
              "text",
              "not"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          "text",
          " create an additional writable data partition, create a persistence session, or perform a managed MiniOS Installer deployment."
        ]
      ]
    ],
    [
      "block",
      "paragraph",
      [
        [
          "text",
          "Persistence after a raw write still depends on the boot mode and writable storage that the resulting image exposes. For a managed target layout or pre-created session, use "
        ],
        [
          "link",
          "/installing-minios/MiniOS-Installer.md",
          null,
          [
            [
              "text",
              "MiniOS Installer"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          "text",
          "."
        ]
      ]
    ],
    [
      "block",
      "paragraph",
      [
        [
          "text",
          "CLI example:"
        ]
      ]
    ],
    [
      "code_block",
      "sudo driveutility-write -s /path/to/minios.iso -t /dev/sdX",
